k\":\"Legend\"}}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L40\",null,{\"href\":\"/tier-list?rank=legend\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-accent hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankTierListLink\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}],\" →\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\",\"name\":\"Cecilion\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"50.39\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Cecilion\",\"delta\":\"-0.71%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.56\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.16\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[\"$La2\",\"$La3\",\"$La4\"]}],\"$La5\",\"$La6\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The Carmilla duo is a distinct draft and should be treated as such. When Carmilla is also on your team, Cecilion unlocks his paired ultimate Moonlit Waltz, which only activates while she is nearby. That ult is the entire reason to play the duo gold lane: Carmilla Curse of Blood links two enemies and pins one in place while Cecilion drops Sanguine Claws into both, and Moonlit Waltz turns Carmilla into a shield around him or a burst-exit missile aimed at a priority target. Without Carmilla, Cecilion is mid only and Moonlit Waltz simply does not appear in his skill bar.\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"If your draft has no reliable hard CC, or if the enemy has two or more of the high-mobility assassins listed above with no peel support on your side, Cecilion is the wrong pick.\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Mana is damage, and damage is patience\"]}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Cecilion's entire kit is an argument for delayed gratification. Every skill scales with his Total Mana, so the pool that Overflowing builds across the game feeds back into every damage number on the page. There is no other hero in the game whose maximum output is unlocked by the game itself.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"This is why Cecilion looks weak through minute 6. He is weak through minute 6. The fantasy of the hero is not early-game combat; it is the moment at minute 14 when his passive has accumulated hundreds of bonus Max Mana from laning, Lightning Truncheon's Resonate procs off the first bat in every fight, and every S1 suddenly chunks a third of a squishy's health instead of a sixth. The hero's job is to survive long enough to become that version of himself. Everything in his kit, from the self-heal on every S3 bolt to the immobilize on Sanguine Claws bought at a shorter cooldown than most hard stuns in the game, exists to keep him alive through the slow half.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Laning: the first six minutes\"]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The goal of laning is not kills. It is mana. Level 1 you take Bat Impact because nothing else matters; wave one is about landing S1 on the minion line twice so you walk into level 2 already carrying Overflowing procs and a growing pool. Level 2, take Sanguine Claws only if you are facing a melee mid who can step onto you (Yin, Chou, Guinevere); otherwise keep pumping S1.\"}]\n85:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Blue buff is non-negotiable.\"}],\" Coordinate with your jungler pre-game. S1's mana cost escalates every time you cast it in quick succession, so a single poke sequence can drain the whole bar. Without blue, one poke sequence dries you. With blue, you can sustain the escalation window twice per wave.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Cast S1 at a steady rhythm, not faster.\"}],\" Overflowing's mana gain runs on its own internal cooldown, so spamming through that window wastes passive procs. Line each cast up with the next wave crash, not the animation recovery. Fast casting feels good and costs mana for nothing.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Flicker is an escape spell, period.\"}],\" With base Movement Speed at 250 and Physical Defense at 17, every river approach is a risk. Reserve Flicker for surviving ganks, not chasing kills. If the enemy jungler is Baxia or Lancelot, drop a ward at mid-river buff before every wave push.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Against a long-range mage (Pharsa, Yve, Xavier), stay at the back of your wave and use Bat Impact's path damage, not the landing hit, to poke. The bat deals damage along its entire path, which means you can fire over your own minions and chunk the enemy without walking into their counter-poke range. The near-landing bonus is a finisher for when someone is already rooted by Sanguine Claws; do not chase it.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The Clock of Destiny plus Lightning Truncheon spike\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Demon Boots, Clock of Destiny, and Lightning Truncheon is the locked opening sequence and the second item is where the hero changes shape. Clock of Destiny gives 400 Mana, 400 HP, and 45 Magic Power at 2030 gold. The mana stat matters more than the Magic Power here: 400 extra Max Mana feeds directly into Overflowing's scaling so every S1 landing hit lands harder before you touch the rest of your stacks. The item's Destiny passive (stacking Hybrid Defense on every damaging skill proc) also provides the sustain Cecilion needs to trade through the exchanges he would otherwise lose. Complete this around minute 6 at worst, minute 5 if your blue schedule is clean.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Lightning Truncheon is the item that flips Cecilion from scaling to winning. Its Resonate passive fires every 6 seconds: the next damaging skill becomes an AoE nuke for 120% Total Magic Power to up to three enemies, plus a 30% movement speed burst that decays over 2 seconds. Layered on top of S1's existing AoE, this means a single Bat Impact now hits for the bat's regular damage plus 120% TMP to everything nearby, with Cecilion sliding forward on the movement burst. Complete Truncheon by minute 8 or 9; any later and your teamfight timing slips behind the enemy's first tower push.\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"After the spike, Cecilion can chunk a squishy for roughly a third of their health with a single S1 landing hit and clear a full back wave from over terrain. This is the moment to stop playing laner and start grouping for first Dragon or a mid-to-bot rotation with your tank. Before the spike, every fight is a gamble. After it, every fight is a countdown.\"}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-4\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning: the wrong reflex\"]}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The reflex when you see Cecilion in a fight is to walk forward into S1 max-stack range because more stacks mean more damage. That reflex is backwards. More stacks inside the fight mean more mana burned on cast, because the cost multiplies with every quick repeat. If you enter the fight cold, you get exactly one useful cast before the rotation decays. If you enter at max stack having pre-stacked on nearby creeps, the first bat already crashes for full damage and every subsequent one layers a Resonate proc on top.\"}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-1\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Pre-stack on jungle camps before every objective.\"}],\" Walk to a nearby camp moments before Dragon or Lord, burn a few S1 casts into the camp creeps, then walk into the objective at max stack with Bats Feast already off cooldown.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Never fire Bats Feast first.\"}],\" The volley sprays in a wide cone, and enemies hit by the first bolt almost always sprint out before the rest connect. Open with Sanguine Claws to immobilize the formation, wait for the root to land, then fire S3 into the frozen cluster.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Angle Sanguine Claws off open lanes, not through walls.\"}],\" The two claws converge from opposite directions, so the spell works best aimed across open lane width. Firing it perpendicular to a wall wastes the far half of the pull. The best cast positions are mid-lane choke, jungle entrance, and the Dragon pit pillars.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n8e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Support-conditional adjustment. If your support is Tigreal or Atlas, push up to stack on creeps near the river because their engage buys you a long cast window at zero risk. If your support is Angela or Diggie, stay one screen behind the frontline and cast from max range; your safety comes from distance, not cover. If your support is Mathilda or Johnson rotating, do not push without the rotation already arriving, because Cecilion has no exit when the roam is elsewhere on the map.\"}]\n8f:[\"$\",\"$La7\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n90:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: three locks, two conversations\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Cecilion has three locked items and then two real conversations. The locked slots are Demon Boots, Clock of Destiny, and Lightning Truncheon, in that order. Demon Boots pays for Mysticism (4% Mana on every minion kill or assist) through laning. Clock of Destiny is the mana pool scaler and the sustain passive. Lightning Truncheon is the teamfight spike. Every build, in every patch, in every matchup, opens with these three.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The first conversation is the flex fourth slot. Three options dominate, and the choice should be made at minute 8 based on the actual game state, not locked in pre-game.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",\"ul-0\",{\"className\":\"list-disc list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Holy Crystal\"}],\" if you are ahead. The Mystery passive grants 21% to 35% bonus Magic Power scaling with hero level, which multiplies with Divine Glaive's penetration at full build. Pick it when you have kills and the enemy mid has no magic defense yet.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Genius Wand\"}],\" if the enemy has stacked magic defense early (Belerick, Gloo, Esmeralda, Barats). The passive shreds Magic Defense on every hit and stacks up to three times, and since Cecilion procs it on every S1 bat, he keeps the stack near-maxed through a poke war. This is the poke-heavy pick and the one most players undervalue.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Glowing Wand\"}],\" if your laning matchup is forcing you below 50% HP often. The 400 HP buffer plus the Scorch burn (1.5% Max HP per second for 3 seconds) stretches your lane time and punishes dive assassins who walk through the fire. The Lifebane passive also cuts enemy shield and HP regen by 50%, which matters against sustain-heavy comps running Esmeralda, Uranus, or a Rafaela support.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The second conversation is the boot slot. Demon Boots stays locked unless you are facing a magic-heavy enemy mid (Chang'e mirror, Xavier, Valentina). In those matchups, Enchanted Talisman replaces Demon Boots as the mana-regen source because Talisman's Mana Spring passive restores 15% of Max Mana every 10 seconds, and Cecilion's Max Mana at two items is already deep enough to make that regeneration meaningful.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Close the build with Divine Glaive and Blood Wings as the standard fifth and sixth. Divine Glaive converts each point of the enemy's Magic Defense into bonus Magic Penetration up to a cap, which is what you need against any enemy sixth-item magic defense. Blood Wings gives Cecilion an 800 plus 100 per Total Magic Power shield and 150 movement speed burst on shield break, neither of which his kit provides.\"}],\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\"]\n91:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Cecilion\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"92:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 bg-surface-3\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6b\",null,{\"src\":\"https://akmweb.youngjoygame.com/web/svnres/img/test/homepage_2_2_16_1232_1/100_d2d28d2fcb060726fa27553920ca1a33.png\",\"alt\":\"Hanzo - Akuma Ninja\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"priority\":\"$undefined\",\"fetchPriority\":\"$undefined\",\"fill\":true,\"className\":\"object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300\",\"sizes\":\"56px\",\"placeholder\":\"blur\",\"blurDataURL\":\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj48cmVjdCB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgZmlsbD0iIzBkMTIyNSIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex-1 min-w-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading font-bold text-text-primary group-hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors truncate\",\"children\":\"Hanzo\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center